   "date": "2013-12-03",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "A motion to refer the Fair Work (Registered Organisations) Amendment Bill 2013 to the Education and Employment References Committee was proposed on behalf of Senator Wong but was blocked by an objection."
  },
  {
   "slug": "speech-826089",
   "speaker": "Claire Moore",
   "party": "Labor",
   "state": "federal",
   "date": "2013-12-03",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The motion to refer the Fair Work (Registered Organisations) Amendment Bill 2013 to the Education and Employment References Committee was moved, arguing that the bill was rushed with only one day of public hearings and that further scrutiny was needed, while opponents cited the government's election mandate and the need for higher penalties for union officials, referencing Justice North's criticism of existing penalties and the support of figures like Paul Howes."
  },
